    "2️⃣ PRESENT PASSIVE YASALISHI\n\nam/is/are + V3 (past participle)\n\nActive: The cleaner cleans the room.\nPassive: The room is cleaned by the cleaner.\n\nActive: People speak English in many countries.\nPassive: English is spoken in many countries.\n\nActive: They grow rice in China.\nPassive: Rice is grown in China.\n\nInkor: is not / are not + V3\n  The room is not cleaned every day.\nSavol: Is/Are + subject + V3?\n  Is English spoken here?",
    "3️⃣ PAST PASSIVE YASALISHI\n\nwas/were + V3 (past participle)\n\nActive: Shakespeare wrote Hamlet.\nPassive: Hamlet was written by Shakespeare.\n\nActive: The children broke the window.\nPassive: The window was broken by the children.\n\nActive: They built this house in 2005.\nPassive: This house was built in 2005.\n\nInkor: was not / were not + V3\n  The window was not broken.\nSavol: Was/Were + subject + V3?\n  When was this house built?",
    "4️⃣ BY + BAJARUVCHI (AGENT)\n\nActive: My mother made this cake.\nPassive: This cake was made by my mother.\n\nBy + bajaruvchi kerak bo'lsa qo'shiladi, kerak bo'lmasa tushiriladi:\n  My bike was stolen. (by someone — kerak emas, noma'lum)\n  English is spoken here. (by people — kerak emas)\n  The Mona Lisa was painted by Leonardo da Vinci. (by + bajaruvchi muhim)",
