    "1️⃣ REPORTED SPEECH NIMA?\n\nDirect speech — kimningdir gapini aynan keltirish:\n  She said: 'I am tired.' (U: 'Men charchadim' dedi)\n\nReported speech — kimningdir gapini o'z so'zlaring bilan aytib berish:\n  She said that she was tired. (U charchaganini aytdi)\n\n📌 SAY vs TELL farqi:\n  say + (that) + clause: He said (that) he was tired.\n  tell + person + (that): He told me (that) he was tired.\n\n  ❌ He told that he was tired. (tell + person kerak: told me / told her)\n  ✅ He said that he was tired. (say ga person kerak emas)",
    "2️⃣ TENSE BACKSHIFT (ZAMAN ORQAGA SILJISHI)\n\nPresent Simple → Past Simple:\n  'I like coffee.' → He said (that) he liked coffee.\n\nPresent Continuous → Past Continuous:\n  'I am reading.' → She said she was reading.\n\nPresent Perfect → Past Perfect:\n  'I have finished.' → He said he had finished.\n\nPast Simple → Past Perfect:\n  'I went home.' → She said she had gone home.\n\nWill → Would:\n  'I will come.' → He said he would come.\n\nCan → Could:\n  'I can swim.' → She said she could swim.\n\n🔴 MUHIM: Agar aytilgan vaqt hali o'tmagan bo'lsa, zamanni o'zgartirmaslik mumkin:\n  'I like coffee.' (haqiqat) → He said he likes coffee. (hali ham to'g'ri)",
    "3️⃣ REPORTED QUESTIONS (SAVOLLAR)\n\nWh- questions:\n  Direct: 'Where do you live?'\n  Reported: He asked where I lived.\n  (So'z tartibi o'zgaradi: Where + subject + lived — do/does KERAK EMAS)\n\nYes/No questions (if/whether):\n  Direct: 'Do you like coffee?'\n  Reported: She asked if I liked coffee.\n  She asked whether I liked coffee.\n\n🔴 QOIDA: Reported question da so'z tartibi o'zgaradi → subject + verb!\n  ❌ He asked where did I live.\n  ✅ He asked where I lived.",
    "4️⃣ REPORTED COMMANDS (BUYRUQLAR)\n\ntell/ask + person + to + V1\n\nDirect: 'Close the door.'\nReported: He told me to close the door.\n  He asked me to close the door.\n\nDirect: 'Don't be late.'\nReported: She told me not to be late.\n  She asked me not to be late.\n\n🔴 QOIDA: Buyruq → tell/ask + person + to + V1\nInkor buyruq → tell/ask + person + not to + V1",
    "5️⃣ SAY VA TELL — BATAFSIL\n\nSay:\n  say + (that) + clause: He said (that) he was tired.\n  say + to + person + (that): He said to me (that) he was tired.\n\nTell:\n  tell + person + (that): He told me (that) he was tired.\n  ❌ He told that (person kerak)\n  ❌ He told to me (to KERAK EMAS)\n\nTime expressions (vaqt so'zlari) o'zgaradi:\n  now → then, today → that day\n  yesterday → the day before / the previous day\n  tomorrow → the next day / the following day\n  here → there, this → that",
